Synthetic task setup
States:
ParseNavigateResolveDoorPickupDeliverInteractDone
Tasks:
goto objectpickup objectopen doorput object near target
The model had to predict the next task state from grid/task features.
Result
Model setupAccuracyIllegal transition rateClassifier without graph/current-state structure86.5%10.5%Same classifier + graph legality mask96.8%0.0%Classifier with current state included99.0%0.0%
That is a good sign.
The graph/state-machine layer was load-bearing when the scorer was weaker: it boosted accuracy from 86.5% to 96.8% and eliminated illegal transitions.
Singularity detector
I flagged the lowest-margin 10% of predictions as “singular / ambiguous.”
RegionAccuracySingular low-margin states81.7%Non-singular states98.5%
That is also what we wanted: the singularity detector identified the part of the state space where the classifier was much less reliable.
What this run proves
It supports the core pipeline:
